{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Adjacent field evidence -- and a variant worth noting for this ticket's scope\n\nObserved 2026-08-05 ~01:45 UTC under parallel agent load on this store.\n\nA completion-sidecar emit lost the race for the store write lock:\n\n    rebar._commands._seam.CommandError: flock: could not acquire lock after 60s\n    at llm/completion_sidecar.py:60 emit -> _commands/_seam.py:419 append_event\n\nWhy this is worth recording HERE specifically: this ticket describes the sidecar being\nSILENTLY lost on write-lock contention, with exit 0 hiding it. In this occurrence the same\ncontention on the same code path surfaced LOUDLY -- a raised CommandError naming flock and\nthe 60s timeout, not a silent exit 0.\n\nSo there appear to be two distinct outcomes from one root condition, and any fix should\naccount for both: a path where the sidecar write fails loudly (this occurrence) and the\npath this ticket reports where it is swallowed. Worth confirming during root-causing whether\nthe difference is the caller (close-gate path vs another), the lock mode, or whether the\nsilent case is specifically a timeout that is caught and discarded further up.\n\nNote the affected close still completed correctly and the ticket carries both plan-review and\ncompletion-verifier attestations -- the loss did not occur here, only the contention."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785894734962442001,"uuid":"58901feb-ef6e-44f9-907d-1af3cb452ae4"}